      "text": "5. Mass of the solution = 80 g\nMass of solute = 16 g\nMass of solvent = $80 - 16 = 64$ g\nAmount of substance dissolved in 64 g water\n= 16 g\nAmount of substance dissolved in 100 g =\n$\\frac{1600}{64} = 25$ g\nSolubility of the substance = 25\nHence, the correct option is (d)."
